# Dagster × OpenTelemetry — Integration Wiki

**Ticket:** CPTO-1016 — Identify OpenTelemetry Integration with Dagster
**Scope:** Dagster OSS on EKS → OpenTelemetry → Grafana

---

## 1. Executive summary

**Question asked:** Airflow can emit Airflow-specific metrics and traces via OTel through a config flag. Does Dagster have an equivalent?

**Answer: No. Dagster OSS has no first-party OpenTelemetry integration of any kind — no metrics, no traces, no logs exporter, and no config flag.**

| Capability | Airflow | Dagster OSS |
|---|---|---|
| Native OTel **metrics** | ✅ `[metrics] otel_on = True` (2.7+) | ❌ none |
| Native OTel **traces** | ✅ `[traces] otel_on = True` (2.10+, experimental) | ❌ none |
| Native OTel **logs** | ⚠️ partial | ❌ none |
| Pre-defined metric catalog | ✅ ~60 documented metrics | ❌ none |
| Community package | — | ❌ no `dagster-opentelemetry` exists |
| Upstream request | — | [#11191](https://github.com/dagster-io/dagster/issues/11191) — **open since Dec 2022**, still unimplemented |

There is no partial support, no deprecated predecessor, and no roadmap commitment. The feature request has been open for over three years.

**Consequence:** every metric we want must be defined and emitted by us. This document specifies which metrics, how to emit them, and how they reach Grafana.

**Recommendation:** proceed in three phases (§9). Phase 1 delivers roughly 60% of operational alerting value with **zero Dagster code changes** and is unblocked today. Phases 2–3 require custom images and pipeline code.

⚠️ **Naming trap for reviewers:** Dagster's docs page `docs.dagster.io/about/telemetry` describes Dagster Labs' own anonymous usage-statistics collection. It is unrelated to observability, and `DAGSTER_DISABLE_TELEMETRY` is not relevant to this ticket.

