## 6. Deployment — Helm values

The official chart has **four** places needing configuration. Missing any one leaves a blind spot; #4 is the one everyone misses.

```yaml
# usw2sandbox-values.yaml

# ---------- 1. Webserver ----------
dagsterWebserver:
  env:
    - { name: OTEL_SERVICE_NAME, value: dagster-webserver }
    - { name: OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT, value: "http://otel-agent.observability.svc.cluster.local:4317" }
    - { name: OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL, value: grpc }
    - { name: OTEL_PYTHON_DISABLED_INSTRUMENTATIONS, value: "sqlalchemy,psycopg2" }
    - { name: OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER, value: parentbased_traceidratio }
    - { name: OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER_ARG, value: "0.1" }
    - { name: OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES, value: "deployment.environment=sandbox,service.namespace=data-platform" }

# ---------- 2. Daemon — run_status_sensors and gauge sensors execute HERE ----------
dagsterDaemon:
  env:
    - { name: OTEL_SERVICE_NAME, value: dagster-daemon }
    - { name: OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT, value: "http://otel-agent.observability.svc.cluster.local:4317" }
    - { name: OTEL_METRIC_EXPORT_INTERVAL, value: "10000" }
    - { name: OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER, value: always_on }   # trace root — never sample away
    - { name: OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES, value: "deployment.environment=sandbox" }

# ---------- 3. Code locations (gRPC servers) ----------
dagster-user-deployments:
  enabled: true
  deployments:
    - name: analytics
      image: { repository: <registry>/analytics, tag: "..." }
      dagsterApiGrpcArgs: ["--module-name", "analytics.definitions"]
      port: 3030
      env:
        - { name: OTEL_SERVICE_NAME, value: dagster-code-analytics }
        - { name: OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT, value: "http://otel-agent.observability.svc.cluster.local:4317" }

# ---------- 4. Run pods — MOST COMMONLY MISSED ----------
# Run pods are created at runtime by the K8sRunLauncher. They do NOT inherit
# chart-level env, and they are invisible to the OTel Operator's mutating
# webhook unless annotated here.
runLauncher:
  type: K8sRunLauncher
  config:
    k8sRunLauncher:
      envVars:                       # NOTE: literal "KEY=VALUE" strings only
        - "OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://otel-agent.observability.svc.cluster.local:4317"
        - "OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL=grpc"
        - "OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=dagster-run"
        - "OTEL_BSP_SCHEDULE_DELAY=1000"
        - "OTEL_METRIC_EXPORT_INTERVAL=5000"
        - "OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER=parentbased_traceidratio"
      envConfigMaps:
        - name: otel-config          # cleaner once there are several code locations
      runK8sConfig:
        podTemplateSpecMetadata:
          annotations:
            instrumentation.opentelemetry.io/inject-python: "dagster/dagster-python"
          labels:
            dagster/observability: "enabled"
        podSpecConfig:
          terminationGracePeriodSeconds: 30   # room for the final flush
```

`envVars` accepts only literal strings — no `valueFrom`. To target the node-local agent instead of the Service (saves a cross-node hop):

```yaml
runK8sConfig:
  containerConfig:
    env:
      - name: NODE_IP
        valueFrom: { fieldRef: { fieldPath: status.hostIP } }
      - name: OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
        value: "http://$(NODE_IP):4317"
```

### 6.1 Process auto-instrumentation

Dagster's long-lived components are ordinary Python processes, so standard auto-instrumentation applies:

| Component | Original | Instrumented |
|---|---|---|
| webserver | `dagster-webserver -h 0.0.0.0 -p 80` | `opentelemetry-instrument dagster-webserver -h 0.0.0.0 -p 80` |
| daemon | `dagster-daemon run` | `opentelemetry-instrument dagster-daemon run` |
| code server | `dagster api grpc -h 0.0.0.0 -p 3030 -m mod` | `opentelemetry-instrument dagster api grpc …` |

This yields GraphQL/HTTP spans from the webserver (useful for "why is Dagit slow") and gRPC spans between daemon and code servers.

> ⚠️ **Disable SQLAlchemy and psycopg2 instrumentation.** Dagster writes hundreds to thousands of event-log rows per run. Full DB span coverage floods the trace backend, costs real money, and measurably slows runs. Set `OTEL_PYTHON_DISABLED_INSTRUMENTATIONS=sqlalchemy,psycopg2` and enable ad hoc only when debugging database issues.

